            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Add the increasing and decreasing sums: each of the n corresponding pairs totals n + 1, then halve.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Write the same sum in increasing and decreasing order.\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=1+2+\\cdots+(n-1)+n\\\\S&=n+(n-1)+\\cdots+2+1\\end{align*}$$\nAdding corresponding terms gives $n$ pairs, each with sum $n+1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2S&=(n+1)+(n+1)+\\cdots+(n+1)\\\\2S&=n(n+1)\\\\S&=\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
